                    {
                      "id": "item:2",
                      "label": "handmade revolver+1<color_c_green> (6/6 .40 S&W JHP)</color>",
                      "description": "Origin: 'Bright Nights'\n--\nMaterial: Steel\nVolume: 0.875 L  Weight: 1.33 kg\nOwner: The Free Merchants\nCategory: GUNS\nWeapon Category: Revolvers, Manual Action\n--\nA sturdy improvised revolver chambered for .38 Special and .357 Magnum.  Its simple design allows for field conversion to 9mm, .40 S&W, .44 Magnum, or .45 ACP with replacement barrel and cylinder assemblies.\n--\nMod: .40 S&W handmade revolver conversion kit (bore) \nA replacement barrel and cylinder assembly for a handmade revolver, converting it to fire .40 S&W cartridges.\n--\nMelee damage: Bash: 8  To-hit bonus: -2\nMoves per attack: 101\nStamina Cost: 110\nTypical damage per second:\nBest: 0.00  Vs. Agile: 0.00  Vs. Armored: 0.00\n--\nAverage melee damage:\nCritical hit chance 4% - 16%\nBashing: 7  Critical bash: 10\nMoves per attack: 67\n--\nBase throw damage: Bash: 9\nThrow damage: Bash: 14\nThrow range: 6\nMoves per throw: 92\nStamina cost: 133\n--\nRanged damage: -1+35 = 34\nMaximum range: 14\nArmor-pierce: 0+0 = 0\nDispersion: 620+50 = 670 (effective: 181)\nSight dispersion: 30+14 = 44\nRecoil percentage: 67\nEffective recoil: 373\nReload time: 285 moves per round\nSkill used: Handguns\nCapacity: 6 rounds of .40\nAmmunition: .40 S&W JHPs\n--\nBase aim speed: 94\nRegular\nEven chance of good hit at range: 3\nTime to reach aim level: 123 moves \nCareful\nEven chance of good hit at range: 4\nTime to reach aim level: 153 moves \nPrecise\nEven chance of good hit at range: 7\nTime to reach aim level: 182 moves \n--\nFire modes: revolver (1)\n--\nMods: 0/2 accessories; 0/1 barrel; 1/1 bore: .40 S&W handmade revolver conversion kit; 0/1 grip; 0/1 rail; 0/1 sights; 0/1 sling; 0/1 stock; 0/1 underbarrel.\n--\nRepair using grid gunsmith repair kit, grid firearm repair kit, gunsmith repair kit, or firearm repair kit.\n* This item can be reinforced.\n--\n* This item conducts electricity.\n* Fouling.  Fouling is caused by firing gunpowder loads repeatedly, which reduces reliability and can eventually cause damage to the gun.  Fouling accumulates slowly (unless blackpowder is used) due to the design of modern smokeless powder found in the vast majority of retail cartridges and it is not a significant problem until high levels of fouling are reached due to firing thousands of rounds without cleaning your firearm.\n--\nCan be stored in: MOLLE pack, power armor XL holster, power armor leg mount, survivor harness, shoulder holster, holster, power armor shoulder holster, power armor holster, survivor MOLLE pack, and XL holster\n--\nPrice: $400.33  Barter value: $8.70\n--\nYou know of nothing you could craft with it.\n",
